<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Time for a flight along a parallel</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>An aircraft flies due [[if test="east"]]east[[else]]west[[/if]] along [[if test="is(ix=1)"]]the parallel \(32^\circ\,\mathrm{N}\) from \(5^\circ\,\mathrm{E}\) to \(40^\circ\,\mathrm{E}\)[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=2)"]]the parallel \(50^\circ\,\mathrm{S}\) from \(20^\circ\,\mathrm{E}\) to \(55^\circ\,\mathrm{E}\)[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=3)"]]the parallel \(20^\circ\,\mathrm{S}\) from \(35^\circ\,\mathrm{E}\) to \(70^\circ\,\mathrm{E}\)[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=4)"]]the parallel \(60^\circ\,\mathrm{N}\) from \(10^\circ\,\mathrm{W}\) to \(30^\circ\,\mathrm{E}\)[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=5)"]]the parallel \(40^\circ\,\mathrm{S}\) from \(60^\circ\,\mathrm{W}\) to \(25^\circ\,\mathrm{W}\)[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=6)"]]the parallel \(25^\circ\,\mathrm{N}\) from \(80^\circ\,\mathrm{W}\) to \(40^\circ\,\mathrm{W}\)[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=7)"]]the parallel \(55^\circ\,\mathrm{S}\) from \(15^\circ\,\mathrm{E}\) to \(40^\circ\,\mathrm{E}\)[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=8)"]]the parallel \(35^\circ\,\mathrm{N}\) from \(50^\circ\,\mathrm{E}\) to \(85^\circ\,\mathrm{E}\)[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=9)"]]the parallel \(45^\circ\,\mathrm{S}\) from \(100^\circ\,\mathrm{E}\) to \(130^\circ\,\mathrm{E}\)[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=10)"]]the parallel \(15^\circ\,\mathrm{N}\) from \(30^\circ\,\mathrm{W}\) to \(5^\circ\,\mathrm{W}\)[[/if]] at \({@v@}\) knots.</p><p>(a) Find the distance it flies, to the nearest nautical mile.</p><p>[[input:ans1]] nm [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p><p>(b) Find the time it takes, to the nearest minute.</p><p>[[input:ans2]] h [[input:ans3]] min [[validation:ans2]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) The difference in longitude is \({@dl@}^\circ = {@60*dl@}'\). Along a parallel, multiply by \(\cos(\text{latitude})\):</p><p>\[{@60*dl@} \times \cos {@phi@}^\circ = {@dispdp(float(nm),1)@} \approx {@floor(nm+1/2)@} \text{ nm}.\]</p><p>(b) Time \(=\) distance \(\div\) speed \(= {@dispdp(float(nm),1)@} \div {@v@} = {@dispdp(float(hrs),3)@}\) h. The decimal part is a fraction of an hour: \({@dispdp(float(hrs-floor(hrs)),3)@} \times 60 = {@dispdp(float(tmin-60*floor(hrs)),1)@}\) min. So the flight takes \({@floor(tr/60)@}\) h \({@mod(tr,60)@}\) min.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
